From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:21:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] u_upload_mgr: release the old buffer when its replacement is
 refused

u_upload_alloc() gives up the full upload buffer for a new one and hands
the old one to the caller to release. When the driver had no memory for
the new buffer it told the caller of no buffer to release, and the
reference the old one held was lost: a context whose uploads were
refused kept every buffer it filled, and recovered none of them. The old
buffer is released at once in that case. A new buffer that could not be
mapped also left the manager pointing at the buffer it had released,
which the next allocation released again; the pointer is cleared.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_upload_mgr.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_upload_mgr.c b/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_upload_mgr.c
index bd2afdd1a07c29f7bfe9216296e802267b30e55e..7a7c4e7614cea9db782cfa72029e68dad0c08bb4 100644
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_upload_mgr.c
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_upload_mgr.c
@@ -207,6 +207,7 @@ u_upload_alloc_buffer(struct u_upload_mgr *upload, unsigned min_size, struct pip
    if (upload->map == NULL) {
       u_upload_release_buffer(upload);
       pipe_resource_release(upload->pipe, upload->buffer);
+      upload->buffer = NULL;
       return 0;
    }
 
@@ -253,6 +254,9 @@ u_upload_alloc(struct u_upload_mgr *upload,
       buffer_size = u_upload_alloc_buffer(upload, offset + size, releasebuf);
 
       if (unlikely(!buffer_size)) {
+         /* The old buffer was given up for one that could not be made, and
+          * the caller is told of no buffer to release: release it here. */
+         pipe_resource_release(upload->pipe, *releasebuf);
          *out_offset = ~0;
          *ptr = NULL;
          *releasebuf = NULL;
